      "note": "Section order, NORM-style heading grammar, and Service-only DbC shape matched what the checker accepted; final authoring receipt was clean (call_00_ET_FQu89FzMDBV9mt55KAur2554)."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "inputs/brief.md lines 5-7 (Input/Outcome table rows)",
      "note": "The two required rows were encoded verbatim in MODULE_REQUIREMENTS, matching the host's required-facts check."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "sdd-check --spec --authoring diagnostic SDD_REQ_ACRONYM_MISMATCH",
      "callId": "call_00_Conq59ANqLO5n1g6ChNt3109",
      "note": "The warning named the exact fix (NORM -> NOR); the second whole-file Write (call_00_S06NHLwrZjTVlgAyx3zL5668) cleared it."
    }
  ],
  "friction": [
    {
      "anchor": "Skeleton SPEC_ID / requirement acronym rule (module-spec-structure.xml, requirement-entry-format.xml)",
      "callId": "call_00_Conq59ANqLO5n1g6ChNt3109",
      "note": "Template gave no visible rule that the requirement acronym is derived from the file name (NOR), not the module name; only the post-write warning revealed it, forcing a second full Write. Could state the derivation in the skeleton comment."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "module.directive.xml#STEP_1_ORIENT / STEP_3_RECONCILE_MAP",
      "callId": "call_00_EPZbh8dcAQeiu1ULKU4l8164",
      "note": "No sdd-orient was run (brief limited scope to deterministic authoring); the repeated rg sweeps for acronym/SPEC_ID rules (also call_01_LhwTlfTuKlKiWOcJQMnl8982) returned nothing and were not needed once the skeleton was read."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "Environment discovery",
      "callId": "call_01_o2cy5zAhxgdMq0J5XH4v6906",
      "note": "`git ls-files && git show --stat HEAD` produced a very large listing that added no authoring information; a narrower `git status` alone would have shown the seeded tree is unchanged."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "Short-lived scaffold",
      "callId": "call_00_vN1eJDbAklsMGsqSQ4vH3251",
      "note": "Post-write grep for leftover placeholders was redundant with the checker's `no-skeleton` result, though harmless."
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Hypothesis: the requirement acronym NOR (file-derived) is the canonical ID prefix while SPEC_ID stays TOKEN-NORMALIZE; checker accepted it, but whether downstream scaffold/trace expects a NOR-* prefix is unknown.",
    "Hypothesis: TypeScript + node-test is an acceptable stack; the brief did not name either, so this remains an assumption recorded in Handoff.",
    "Unknown whether the first Write's content would have passed had the acronym been spelled NOR initially; that was not measured.",
    "Unknown whether the second read of the target (call_00_EC7wNwoBYqT4oaB62od25176) was strictly necessary; it was used to confirm checker auto-fix left the body unchanged before the acronym rewrite."
  ],
  "nextHypothesis": "Test adding an explicit acronym-derivation line to the module skeleton comment (e.g. `requirement acronym = derived from spec file name`), predicting the first Write passes sdd-check with zero warnings and removes one whole-file rewrite; also test whether a brief-level stack declaration removes the Handoff assumption."
}
